<title>TURKEY: Turkish Eregli 1996 profits fall.</title>
<headline>Turkish Eregli 1996 profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final results</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)     964.24  vs    1,386.72</p>
<p>    Net profit		    6,109.44  vs    8,786.28</p>
<p>    Net sales		    73,704.78  vs   33,826.17</p>
<p>    Operating Profits	  18,396.29  vs    9,913.16</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  3,671.29  vs    6,310.63</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	 1,095.95  vs	314.71</p>
<p>    Interest Paid		11,536.48  vs    4,344.09</p>
<p>    Extraordinary expense     2,578.30  vs    1,574.33</p>
<p>    Total debts		 101,441.72  vs   52,289.49</p>
<p>    Equity			 38,551.54  vs   25,482.64</p>
<p>    Capital			 6,336.00  vs    6,336.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's largely state-onwed flat steel giant Eregli Demir Celik Fabrikalari T.A.S. is slated for privatisation, with 51.66 percent of its capital held by the privatisation administration OIB.</p>
<p>The company plans to pay 453.7 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal valued share from its 1996 profits after approval at the annual meeting of shareholders and directors on March 27.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
